{"id":200,"event":"agent","data":{"type":"text_delta","delta":": **`voicebox/` repo + `voicebox.sh` public docs**, not Gnani’s commercial page.\n\n<od-card type=\"task-brief\">\n{ \"summary\": \"Local Windows-native Voicebox control surface — real API, real profiles, zero mocked data.\", \"fields\": [ {\"label\": \"Audience\", \"value\": \"you, local Voicebox user\"}, {\"label\": \"Deliverable\", \"value\": \"production-grade live artifact per screen\"}, {\"label\": \"Source of truth\", \"value\": \"pick-of-gods/voicebox repo + local FastAPI at 127.0.0.1:17493\"}, {\"label\": \"Out of scope\", \"value\": \"cloud backup, $VOICEBOX token, pricing, SaaS auth\"} ] }\n</od-card>\n\nConcrete screen map from the actual repo (each is a separate HTML file per `screen-file-first rule`):\n\n1. **`index.html`** — launcher overview: local server status, quick-start actions, recent activity\n2. **`profiles.html`** — voice profile list + create/delete/select real profiles via `GET /api/profiles`, `POST /api/profiles`\n3. **`clone.html`** — real voice cloning flow: record/or upload sample → name/profile → hit `POST /api/profiles`\n4. **`generate.html`** — TTS generation: pick profile, enter text, select engine, hit `POST /api/generations`, play result\n5. **`history.html`** — real generation history via `GET /api/generations`, play/download\n6. **`captures.html`** — capture list + audio gateway via `GET /api/captures`\n7. **`server.html`** — local server settings via `GET /api/settings`, engine routing, restart\n\n**Which screen do you want first, and do you want the existing Vue app adapted or a fresh Windows-native control surface?** The Tauri shell already exists; I can build against `127.0.0.1:17493` directly from either the existing React frontend or a standalone control page."},"timestamp":1783670605839}
